{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact CF-1 head ffcaf60c33d69114961083ca2b51b90d750046c9 on builder/cf1-cutover-family-20261113, with carried TM-1 commit 51e88288, all 100 artifacts, for review request 60a32cd6 under CF-1 promise e9455ef9 and TM-1 promise 11483fc4. The base family does what the note says. Its new authority stays narrow, the creation marker reads the same in runtime and replay, and the gate evidence holds.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- Creation marker, `packages/derive/src/creation-context.ts`. Version 3 admits exactly `{ v, publication }` or `{ v, publication, delegate, deviceCommand }`. The list holds 1 to 8 strictly ascending texts of at most 256 bytes, and the device grant gets the same root and definition checks as v2. A device grant alone stays v2. The genesis judge (`genesis.ts:193`), the send path (`sends.ts:132`), the device capability (`capability/device-command.ts:25`) and the provenance check (`publishing-provenance.ts:207`) all call this one function, so runtime and replay admit the same genesis. `creation-context.test.ts` refuses 13 malformed markers, and a child of a v3 root gets v1 or v2, never the prefixes.\n- Membership 14, `base-membership.ts`.\n  - `revoke-key-authority`, `own-member` and `remove-member-authority` run only when no `membership.manage` grant holds. Each finds the signer's active key of an active member.\n  - A key may revoke only itself, and a person may act only on an active agent whose recorded controller is that person.\n  - `last-admin-kept` now skips its check only when `signedByRecovery` holds. So self-revoke and `leave` keep the last admin, and the test at line 57 witnesses both.\n  - `own-agent-keys` counts invited and active keys in the state before the act and refuses at the fifth.\n- Publication prefixes, `publication-paths.ts`.\n  - A prefix ends in one slash. It has no empty, dot, `..` or `.git` segment, no glob or control character, and no backslash, and it doesn't start with `.github/`.\n  - Overlap compares whole strings with their trailing slash, so `shelf/` and `shelf-other/` don't collide.\n  - `withinPublicationPrefixes` refuses any path with an empty or dot segment.\n- Directory 27, `base-directory.ts`. `publication-prefix-free` checks each `creating` or `created` application, so a refused or conflicting creation releases its claim. The root's seed takes the delivery cause (`application-install-creation.ts:91-92`), so each creation has its own scope ID. A refused creation's `application-paths` row therefore names a scope that can never exist, and that row grants nothing. `has-repository` now reads the act's own repository item.\n- Destination 21, `base-destination.ts`. Only the Directory of the branch can open an `application-paths` row (`not-the-directory`). `publish-file` refuses a path outside the sender's row and holds while no row exists.\n- The host check, `destination-host.ts:663-667` and `publication-policy.ts`. With `scopePublicationPrefixesDestination`, the host checks every touched path and every link target against the same rows before it pushes. A link that doesn't resolve counts as outside, and a sender that isn't a scope reference stops the push.\n- Rules 15, `base-rules.ts`. An ordinary package must name no owner, and a device package must name an active owner. The installation genesis keeps the prefixes, and the creation request carries them to the Directory. Host admission (`applications/admission.ts:37`) now admits any capability set that `applicationCapabilities` reads, and each room's Rules pin still judges its own sets.\n- TM-1, `51e88288`. It changes three timeouts in three test files and nothing else: residency 162 s, one thousand births `scaleDeadline(990000)` and G15 275 s, as ruling 67cafb4d accepts. Attempt 3 measured 58.3 s, 251.3 s and 84.7 s, each under a third of its limit.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main a200cd0a is an ancestor, and the pushed branch equals the head. Against main, the head changes 97 paths, and the 100 artifacts cover every one: the primary, 96 path artifacts and the three TM-1 report artifacts. The primary is neither stale nor retired.\n- Source correspondence. `git diff --name-only 4369fddf ffcaf60c` lists only Markdown files and the manifest. Merge 8cd68d3e has parents 4369fddf and a200cd0a. It resolves one conflict in `docs/cli.md`, which stays documentation. So every source, test, configuration and dependency file at the head equals the gate checkpoint.\n- Evidence. The manifest's digest is 9edd8b4c, as the request states. All 43 files that it lists match their SHA-256 values, and `SHA256SUMS` (cf8c9f21) verifies. `gate.exit` is 0, `head.txt` names 4369fddf with tree da0bdbb8, and `gate.stdout` ends \"gate passed\" with no timeout line. All 81 power samples, from 22:42 to 23:08 EST, read AC Power, and power mode is 0 at START and END. The host's `pmset -g log` shows no sleep or wake from 22:40 to 23:12.\n- Cheap checks at the head. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, the commit-message check passes (14 checked, 0 flagged), `git diff --check` is clean, and `check-doc-links` finds 1,245 links with 0 broken.\n- Seal, on my own clone at the head. `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs` passes 12 of 12. I ran no other tests.\n\nKernel review under `docs/kernel.md` section 7: no objection. The one kernel change is the v3 marker in `packages/derive/src/creation-context.ts`, which ruling bccd8dd1 permits. The genesis judge reads the marker through the one function that replay also runs. The five pins are new versions of existing platform names, so they add five to K1's count. The head adds no platform name and no member of `RefusalReason`. The four refusal names are guard and grant names of Native rules.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One family is the default for every host, and older families stay explicit choices. The prefixes travel in one direction: package, Rules, Directory claim, root marker, Destination row, host check. Each step reads the record of the step before it, so replay derives each refusal. The Directory and the Destination learn the prefixes in the same entry that requests the creation.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The new self branches only remove the signer's own standing, and a controller acts only on its own agents. The recovery key is the one route past `last-admin`. Prefix claims are exclusive. The Destination and the host each check every path and link target, so an application can't publish outside its declared directories through a symlink or a later change. Three notes for later work:\n\n1. `revoke-key-authority` lets a person revoke a key of their own agent without the check that `remove-member-authority` makes for the action `membership.own-agent`. The note says that the person \"who holds `membership.own-agent`\" may do both. Revoking only removes authority, so the code is safe. Make the note and the file header say the same thing in a later head.\n2. Prefixes compare by exact bytes. `Shelf/` and `shelf/` are two claims, and so are two Unicode normalizations of one name. That is safe on GitHub, which is case-sensitive, but on a case-insensitive checkout the two directories are one. A later Rules version could compare a case-folded, normalized form.\n3. An `application-paths` row is kept for every creation, refused ones included, up to 1,000. That limit matches the Directory's application limit, so a full table of rows needs as many installs by an admin.\n\nSimplification: no required change. `installedApplicationOrigin` now carries three marker branches: `capabilities`, `deviceCommand` and none. When the older device families retire, the `capabilities` branch can replace the other two.\n\nThis approval authorizes no landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing. CDF-1 must land before the cutover deployment, as the note's open limits state.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6c7c6534a251cd765243818dbeb77b20a3bc4bd4","binding":"assigned","head":"ffcaf60c33d69114961083ca2b51b90d750046c9","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:75c8d0ac7ecadf1f503c593a6accc39b816a1370\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e9455ef9e47fd065cd07ee94c3b0da9c05427c7b\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:11483fc4ac1385e0b319ab31d042893de687c60e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cac2319e61cc8822043d0581f326b42ea25bcf9c","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}